36TRAV01533M_.JPG","at":"2026-11-22T20:20:37","link":"/raw_images/1657590"},{"rover":"Perseverance","zh":"毅力號","sol":2031,"cam":"SuperCam zoom","camZh":"超級相機","src":"https://mars.nasa.gov/mars2020-raw-images/pub/ods/surface/sol/02031/ids/edr/browse/scam/LRF_2031_0847235763_228EBY_N0930000SCAM01031_0010I4J01_1200.jpg","at":"2026-11-06T11:41:23","link":"https://mars.nasa.gov/mars2020/multimedia/raw-images/LRF_2031_0847235763_228EBY_N0930000SCAM01031_0010I4J"},{"rover":"Perseverance","zh":"毅力號","sol":2031,"cam":"SuperCam zoom","camZh":"超級相機","src":"https://mars.nasa.gov/mars2020-raw-images/pub/ods/surface/sol/02031/ids/edr/browse/scam/LRF_2031_0847236596_261EBY_N0930000SCAM01031_0050I4J01_1200.jpg","at":"2026-11-06T11:55:16","link":"https://mars.nasa.gov/mars2020/multimedia/raw-images/LRF_2031_0847236596_261EBY_N0930000SCAM01031_0050I4J"},{"rover":"Curiosity","zh":"好奇號","sol":5082,"cam":"ChemCam zoom","camZh":"化學相機","src":"https://mars.nasa.gov/msl-raw-images/proj/msl/redops/ods/surface/sol/05082/opgs/edr/ccam/CR0_848639173EDR_F1260000CCAM03081M_.JPG","at":"2026-11-22T18:19:23","link":"/raw_images/1657550"},{"rover":"Perseverance","zh":"毅力號","sol":2031,"cam":"SuperCam zoom","camZh":"超級相機","src":"https://mars.nasa.gov/mars2020-raw-images/pub/ods/surface/sol/02031/ids/edr/browse/scam/LRF_2031_0847237865_241EBY_N0930000SCAM01031_0100I4J01_1200.jpg","at":"2026-11-06T12:16:25","link":"https://mars.nasa.gov/mars2020/multimedia/raw-images/LRF_2031_0847237865_241EBY_N0930000SCAM01031_0100I4J"},{"rover":"Curiosity","zh":"好奇號","sol":5082,"cam":"ChemCam zoom","camZh":"化學相機","src":"https://mars.nasa.gov/msl-raw-images/proj/msl/redops/ods/surface/sol/05082/opgs/edr/ccam/CR0_848639906EDR_F1260000CCAM03081M_.JPG","at":"2026-11-22T18:31:36","link":"/raw_images/1657551"}],"apod":{"date":"2026-11-22","title":"Swirls and Colors on Jupiter from Juno","text":"What creates the colors in Jupiter's clouds? No one is sure. The thick atmosphere of Jupiter is mostly hydrogen and helium, elements which are colorless at the low temperatures of the Jovian cloud tops. Which trace molecules provide the colors remains a topic of research, although small amounts of ammonium hydrosulfide are one leading candidate. What is clear from the featured color-enhanced image -- and many similar images -- is that lighter clouds are typically higher up than darker ones. Pictured, light clouds swirl around reddish regions toward the lower right, while they appear to cover over some darker domains on the upper right. The featured image was taken by the robotic Juno spacecraft in 2018 during its 14th low pass over Jupiter. Juno continues in its looping elliptical orbit, swooping near the huge planet every 33 days and exploring a slightly different sector each time around.","img":"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/JupiterSwirls_JunoBrealey_3709.jpg?w=1400&fit=clip","by":"NASA, Juno, SwRI, MSSS; Processing & License : Matt Brealey, Seán Doran","video":false},"tle":["1 25544U 98067A   26326.55861648  .00009004  00000+0  16808-3 0  9990","2 25544  51.6321 236.3579 0007404  53.9088 306.2585 15.49552037596306"],"passes":[{"start":"2026-11-23T17:36:56Z","end":"2026-11-23T17:41:32Z","top":"2026-11-23T17:40:17Z","max":90,"from":["W","西"],"to":["E","東"],"mins":5},{"start":"2026-11-23T19:13:45Z","end":"2026-11-23T19:14:28Z","top":"2026-11-23T19:16:56Z","max":41,"from":["W","西"],"to":["W","西"],"mins":1},{"start":"2026-11-24T16:48:56Z","end":"2026-11-24T16:55:39Z","top":"2026-11-24T16:52:17Z","max":87,"from":["W","西"],"to":["E","東"],"mins":7},{"start":"2026-11-24T18:25:44Z","end":"2026-11-24T18:28:39Z","top":"2026-11-24T18:29:01Z","max":55,"from":["W","西"],"to":["SW","西南"],"mins":3},{"start":"2026-11-25T17:37:43Z","end":"2026-11-25T17:42:31Z","top":"2026-11-25T17:41:03Z","max":69,"from":["W","西"],"to":["SE","東南"],"mins":5},{"start":"2026-11-25T19:14:47Z","end":"2026-11-25T19:15:30Z","top":"2026-11-25T19:17:27Z","max":22,"from":["W","西"],